1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,960
This is the story of NVIDIA,

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:05,500
and one investment idea.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,870
Today, millions of people use AI.

4
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,000
You ask a question.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,290
A computer answers.

6
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:18,930
Even an 80-year-old retiree uses it.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,790
NVIDIA was started in 1993 by Jensen Huang.

8
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:29,200
At first, it made chips for video games.

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,130
These chips are called GPUs.

10
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:37,730
A regular chip does a few jobs at a time.

11
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:41,710
A GPU does thousands of jobs at once.

12
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,730
That is exactly what AI needs.

13
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:50,120
Here is why NVIDIA is so important.

14
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,410
Think of a gold rush.

15
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:56,010
The people who sold the shovels did very well.

16
00:00:57,010 --> 00:01:00,750
In the AI rush, NVIDIA sells the shovels: the chips.

17
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:04,880
The biggest tech companies buy them to build their AI.

18
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:10,170
These chips fill giant computer buildings,

19
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:12,490
called data centers.

20
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:14,980
That is where AI lives.

21
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:19,530
So, let's connect the dots.

22
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:22,170
Games led to GPUs.

23
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,720
GPUs power AI.

24
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:29,010
And AI needs data centers full of NVIDIA chips.

25
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,850
And the business is growing fast.

26
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:39,700
In three recent quarters, sales went from $68.1 billion,

27
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,490
to $81.6 billion,

28
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,310
to $96.2 billion.

29
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,780
Many large companies work with NVIDIA.

30
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:54,670
Soon, NVIDIA will report its next results.

31
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:58,070
Results like these can move the share price.

32
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:02,770
Now, the investment idea.

33
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:06,180
A share costs $218.

34
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:09,000
If the price rises 8%,

35
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,880
it becomes $235.44.

36
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,860
The idea uses borrowed money, called leverage.

37
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:23,500
You put in $25,000 of your own.

38
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,010
The broker lends you about $100,000 more.

39
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:31,940
Together, you buy 572 shares.

40
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:37,810
By investing $25,000 this way,

41
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:44,900
you could potentially make $9,975.68.

42
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:49,820
With $50,000 of your own,

43
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,140
and more borrowed money,

44
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:56,290
you buy 1,720 shares.

45
00:02:57,290 --> 00:03:03,240
That could potentially make $29,996.80.

46
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:07,230
Just remember:

47
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:11,780
borrowed money also makes losses bigger if the price falls.

48
00:03:14,770 --> 00:03:18,590
NVIDIA: the company selling the shovels of the AI age.
